Find K-Largest 	--> Min Heap
Find K-Smallest --> Max Heap

Sum of numbers 1..𝑛 --> n(n+1)/2
Number of subarrays of size 𝑛 --> n(n+1)/2
Number of ways to choose 2 elements from 𝑛 elements --> n(n-1)/2

Heap:
----
It is a binary tree (each node can have at most two children) that follows the heap property. In a min heap, Parent ≤ Children and in max heap Parent ≥ Children.

• Min Heap: Queue<Integer> minHeap = new PriorityQueue<>();
• Max Heap: 
Queue<Integer> maxHeap = new PriorityQueue<>(Collections.reverseOrder());
OR
Queue<Integer> maxHeap = new PriorityQueue<>((a, b) -> b - a);

Map:
---
• Unordered:
Map<Integer, Integer> map = new HashMap<>();

• Ordered:
TreeMap<Integer, Integer> map = new TreeMap<>();

Here by default the map is sorted by key in ascending order.

○ To sort in descending order:
TreeMap<Integer, Integer> map = new TreeMap<>((a, b) -> b - a);

Note: Here a and b are keys and not values.

• Sort by value (using heap)
Queue<Map.Entry<Character, Integer>> sortByValueMap = new PriorityQueue<>((e1, e2) -> e1.getValue() - e2.getValue());
sortByValueMap.addAll(myMap.entrySet());

Set:
---
Unordered:
Set<Integer> set = new HashSet<>();

Ordered:
Ascending: TreeSet<Integer> set = new TreeSet<>();
Descending: TreeSet<Integer> set = new TreeSet<>((a, b) -> Integer.compare(b, a));

Common Templates:
----------------
for (Map.Entry<Integer, Integer> e : map.entrySet()) {
    int key = e.getKey();
    int val = e.getValue();
}

Use map.keySet() to iterate over keys

Sort array:
----------
Arrays.sort(arr);
Arrays.sort(arr, Collections.reverseOrder());

Note: For primitive arrays (int[], char[]) you CANNOT use comparator directly. For e.g. below line of code will not work.
Arrays.sort(arr, (a, b) -> b - a); // compile error

Workaround: use Integer[]
Integer[] arr = {5, 2, 8, 1};

Arrays.sort(arr, (a, b) -> b - a); // descending

Sort ArrayList:
--------------
Collections.sort(list); // ascending
Collections.sort(list, (a, b) -> Integer.compare(b, a)); // descending
OR
list.sort((a, b) -> Integer.compare(b, a));

Sorting objects:
---------------
List<int[]> list = new ArrayList<>();

list.sort((a, b) -> a[1] - b[1]);
